<description>&lt;p&gt;Egypt reopened its embassy in Tripoli, restoring diplomatic ties after a 12‑year gap. ISIS militants killed a young Christian man in Libya after he refused to deny Jesus. A fire triggered an explosion at a gas complex in Marsa Brega, killing one worker and injuring four, while authorities detained a translator and arrested a man in Tripoli for throwing grenades at the army. Libya and Chad signed the final document of the CEN SAD Executive Council meeting, and combat intensity remains low, with 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxOUmxJSTBtNC0zNWtPUkRhQ1JxS2dCRndtN3o1cURid3ZkdTRjTmthSmRubHJONFNBYlFLT1MwVGVyUENyNnYyYTU3Rnp5YjRSa3Z0NWprOWl6ckx4T3hXS3dGeThhZjlzWHFZSDNrX2VabUlaZWhKQUJORlJBYlFqNTJNYWRCaWcxLWhDTkxIRVl2Q2JvYlFVajdlN050dlI0?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxNU0Y3N3dwVkdGV1BpRmwxQ0FIYmYxVlRabkE2VU96bEVLMVhGVG01VTd6VDdpWFM0bktUSTZJczFsX2pHWWZ6SjN3RUVBbGRwaGJJUWtOUUFWcW1CUVV6bzItdjNHVm0zUmJ5VEI4RVhDLUV2RFV4Z3d5NGphSER3cXFBTHg3RDV3Smg4c0tUTVFTUHg0X2paSmRORWk?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiSEFVX3lxTE1Ma0oyRTlFR0toN2Vyd3pEbWlsYnBObFJyZE9QTGZLYlJpU2RMdEs3VUlCREtVVjlCZHNtZ3RfUEpudVV1T0hIQg?oc=5&quot;&gt;سانا&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxPQmVJQ1Vsak9BN3VYOWlQWXZvNURQWXdBM2pZQmJPZkd2THQ1ekNMNkF5MnJkLU9jbXNoUkVkNVVoeGRMV0RuRHpPdmpRNzBScVFHZ3ozMmtsWXlPclFES0U5R3pTQmlwOWlUSUl0NVhyc0hDVGIxbF9HNjVJYmFYem5YYWJSS2Vrd3Mtekl5Tmd0TS05NDVkcmJ1dHdHNHFu?oc=5&quot;&gt;www.christiantoday.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMioAFBVV95cUxObHlZbHVyU0ZJd0l1a